---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "../lib/urls";
---

<BaseLayout title="About — BOHUC" description="From a desk at home to an independent leather workshop—the story behind BOHUC.">
  <header class="about-hero">
    <div class="page-width about-hero__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">OUR STORY / 2018 — TODAY</p>
        <h1>One pair of hands.<br />A little more room.</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="about-hero__intro">
        <p>BOHUC began at a small desk with a cutting mat, a borrowed lamp, and a desire to understand how good leather goods are made.</p>
        <p>The workshop has grown since then. The pace, attention, and belief in making every piece by hand have not.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="about-story" aria-labelledby="about-story-title">
    <div class="page-width">
      <div class="about-story__heading" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">FROM THEN TO NOW</p>
        <h2 id="about-story-title">A workshop built slowly.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="about-timeline">
        <article class="about-chapter" data-reveal>
          <figure class="about-chapter__image">
            <div class="about-chapter__frame">
              <img
                src={withBase("images/about/before.jpg")}
                alt="The first BOHUC work desk at home with leather tools, patterns and a cutting mat"
                width="826"
                height="1100"
                loading="eager"
              />
            </div>
            <figcaption>Where the first pieces were made.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="about-chapter__copy">
            <p class="about-chapter__year">2018</p>
            <p class="about-chapter__lead">A desk at home, a cutting mat and a borrowed lamp.</p>
            <p>I finished university that year with no plan to make anything. A worn-out wallet I tried to repair turned into months of reading, testing, and learning how leather behaves.</p>
            <p>By the end of the year I had gathered a beginner's set of tools—a round knife, an awl, two needles, and a block of wax—and cleared a desk at home to use them on. For the next few years, every piece was made after work and on weekends.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="about-chapter about-chapter--reverse" data-reveal>
          <figure class="about-chapter__image">
            <div class="about-chapter__frame">
              <img
                src={withBase("images/about/after.jpg")}
                alt="The BOHUC leather workshop today with cutting tables, tools and sewing equipment"
                width="1600"
                height="1200"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </div>
            <figcaption>More room, the same careful process.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="about-chapter__copy">
            <p class="about-chapter__year">2021</p>
            <p class="about-chapter__lead">The workshop today—same knife, more room.</p>
            <p>In 2021 I left my job and gave the work all of my week. The desk at home became a proper workshop, with enough space to cut, stitch, finish, and photograph each piece.</p>
            <p>Nothing important about the making changed: the same measured pace, the same two-needle stitch, and still one pair of hands responsible from beginning to end. BOHUC is a workshop, not a production line—and it was never meant to become one.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-belief" data-reveal>
    <div class="page-width about-belief__grid">
      <p class="eyebrow">WHAT HASN'T CHANGED</p>
      <blockquote>Make fewer things.<br />Make them well.<br />Let them age with you.</blockquote>
      <a class="button about-belief__button" href={withBase("how-its-made/")}>See how it's made</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
